@@ -0,0 +1,2113 @@
+flf2a$ 20 16 34 0 30 0
+Modified by Paul Burton September 96 from caligraphy.flf as a demonstration of 
+FigWin features.  Modification took about 5 minutes using FigWin's "rectangle 
+search and replace" feature.  The characters previously consisted of only "*" 
+characters.  These changes required two steps:
+
+First, all instances of "*" were replaced with "#" to give the font a darker 
+appearance.  
+
+                         #                      /
+Then, all instances of: #  were replaced with: /   (Each of these is a 
+rectangle of four squares, including two blanks.)
+
+Also added a period, exclamation point, and question mark and changed the 
+default smushmode.
+
+Original caligraphy.flf composed by Vinney Thai October 94
+ -----------------------------=<< FigWin Hype >>=------------------------------
+ These comments were generated automatically by FigWin, not the author of the
+ font.  FigWin is the Windows clone of FIGlet with a full featured font editor!
+ Forget about doing the math to figure out the smushmode number!  Just check a
+ few boxes for each smushing rule.  Forget about endmarks!  Let the computer
+ figure out how tall and how wide your font is.  Just draw fonts with the mouse
+ and wipe the smudgemarks off your screen from all that counting!
+
+ FigWin is full of features, but it's designed for use by a complete idiot.  If
+ you qualify, visit the FigWin website.  Screen shots are shown, and of course
+ you will be able to download it.
+
+                      http://home.earthlink.net/~solution
